  <notes>FR-D5. DONE 2026-08-06 (owner-approved full paired slice; file-scope lifted). Layers:
    (1) BFF — added minimal `RestoredUploadedFile(FileId,FileName,ContentType,SizeBytes)` projection to
    `RestoredSession` + `SessionRestoreService` (projects the ALREADY-loaded `StoredSession.UploadedFiles`;
    ADR-040 no new store/query) + `SessionRestoreUploadedFileDto` on `SessionRestoreResponse` mapped in
    `RestoreSessionAsync`. Enriched fields (SummaryText/Sections/Citations/ExtractedText) deliberately
    excluded (ADR-015 Tier-2). 3 unit tests (`SessionRestoreServiceUploadedFilesTests`) pass. BFF build
    clean; publish 46.97 MB compressed incl PDBs (≤60, no package delta).
    (2) Client — `useSessionRestore.ts` `SessionRestoreSpec.uploadedFiles` (+backward-compat normalize);
    `ThreePaneShell` RestoreContextValue += `sessionId` + `uploadedFiles`; `ConversationPane` reads
    `restoreCtx.uploadedFiles`, gates on `chatSessionId===restoreCtx.sessionId` + live-count==0, renders the
    restored chip through the SAME host-owned `FilesAttachedIndicator`.
    SprkChat `initialAttachments` seam AVOIDED (coordinator's sanctioned fallback): seeding
    `useChatFileAttachment` would re-fire `onAttachmentsChanged` → useAttachments ready-transition
    side-effects (spurious "File attached" msgs, `files_staged` dispatch, task-024 new-session prompt on a
    restored session that has prior messages). Shared lib `@spaarke/ui-components` UNTOUCHED (ADR-012) — no
    rebuild needed. typecheck Surface-owned:0; 618/618 ConvPane Jest tests pass incl new
    `ConversationPane.restore-attachment-chip.test.tsx` (chip shows / empty-hidden / session-gated / dark-mode
    ADR-021). Step 9.5 code-review + adr-check: 0 Critical, 0 violations. NOT committed (orchestrator does the
    consolidated build+commit). NOTE: this rehydrates the COLD-LOAD restore path (`/restore` via
    useSessionRestore); the in-session History-menu reopen (035's `/tabs`+loadHistory, WorkspacePane-owned) is
    a separate carrier not covered here.</notes>
